{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.18, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 24, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:02:57.796Z", "t_ms": 6177, "delta": "Both GraphRAG and RAPTOR build hierarchical, multi-level summaries to facilitate retrieval"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.503, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 25, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:02:58.117Z", "t_ms": 6499, "delta": " across large corpora, but they rely on fundamentally different structural representations and grouping mechanisms:\n\n### GraphRAG\n* **Knowledge"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.62, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 26, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:02:58.235Z", "t_ms": 6617, "delta": " Graph Construction:** GraphRAG first extracts key entities (as nodes) and their relationships (as edges) from the source"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.839, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 27, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:02:58.454Z", "t_ms": 6836, "delta": " text using an LLM [C2].\n* **Hierarchical Community Partitioning:** Rather than clustering raw text chunks"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.088, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 28, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:02:58.703Z", "t_ms": 7084, "delta": ", it detects modular, nested communities of closely related entities across the graph structure using graph partitioning algorithms [C1, C2"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.23, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 29, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:02:58.845Z", "t_ms": 7227, "delta": ", C3].\n* **Bottom-Up Summarization:** Summaries are generated hierarchically using an LLM [C2"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.423, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 30, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:02:59.038Z", "t_ms": 7420, "delta": "]:\n  * *Leaf-level communities:* Element descriptions (source and target nodes, edges, and related claims) are"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.624, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 31, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:02:59.239Z", "t_ms": 7621, "delta": " prioritized by node degree prominence and packed into the context window up to the token limit [C7].\n  * *"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.836, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 32, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:02:59.451Z", "t_ms": 7833, "delta": "Higher-level communities:* If all elements fit within the context window, they are summarized directly; otherwise, sub-community summaries"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.109, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 33, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:02:59.724Z", "t_ms": 8105, "delta": " are recursively substituted in place of their longer constituent element summaries to fit the context limit [C7].\n* **Retrie"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.252, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 34, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:02:59.867Z", "t_ms": 8249, "delta": "val Role:** These community-level summaries provide thematic, corpus-wide overviews that are queried via a map-reduce procedure"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.428, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 35, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:03:00.043Z", "t_ms": 8425, "delta": " to answer broad sensemaking questions [C2].\n\n### RAPTOR\n* **Chunking and Dense Embeddings:** RAP"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.926, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 36, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:03:00.541Z", "t_ms": 8923, "delta": "TOR divides the source text into short, contiguous chunks of 100 tokens (preserving sentence boundaries) and computes dense"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.937, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 37, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:03:00.552Z", "t_ms": 8934, "delta": " vector representations using SBERT embeddings to serve as leaf nodes [C14].\n* **Embedding-Based Clustering:** Text chunks are"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.177, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 38, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:03:00.792Z", "t_ms": 9174, "delta": " grouped semantically (rather than by their physical order or adjacency in the text) using UMAP dimensionality reduction combined with Gaussian Mixture"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.269, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 39, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:03:00.884Z", "t_ms": 9266, "delta": " Models (GMMs) [C9, C10, C14]. It utilizes soft clustering, enabling"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.446, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 40, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:03:01.061Z", "t_ms": 9443, "delta": " text segments to belong to multiple clusters simultaneously [C10].\n* **Recursive Tree Construction:** An LLM (such"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.6, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 41, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:03:01.215Z", "t_ms": 9596, "delta": " as GPT-3.5-turbo) summarizes each cluster of text chunks [C5, C14]. The resulting summary"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.959, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 42, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:03:01.573Z", "t_ms": 9955, "delta": " texts are re-embedded, reclustered, and summarized again recursively until further clustering is no longer feasible, forming a multi-layered tree"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.154, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 43, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:03:01.769Z", "t_ms": 10150, "delta": " [C14].\n* **Retrieval Role:** Both the original text leaves and the intermediate/higher-level summary nodes are indexed"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.342, "data": {"request_id": "3abb811d311c", "seq": 44, "ts": "2026-10-28T07:03:01.957Z", "t_ms": 10339, "delta": " together and queried using either layer-by-layer tree traversal or collapsed-tree retrieval [C12, C14]."}}
